{"id":"mahabharata-7-111","work":"mahabharata","part":7,"partName":"द्रोणपर्व","partNameEn":"Drona Parva","unit":111,"title":"एकादशाधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 111 · Karna in rage; the duel goes on","summary":{"en":"Seeing Dhritarashtra's sons fallen, Karna rages and fights Bhima with arrows and counter-arrows. The two warriors, smeared with blood and wounds, shine like blazing mountains.","kn":"ಧೃತರಾಷ್ಟ್ರನ ಮಕ್ಕಳು ಬಿದ್ದುದನ್ನು ಕಂಡು ಕರ್ಣ ಕೆರಳಿ ಬಾಣ-ಪ್ರತಿಬಾಣಗಳಿಂದ ಭೀಮನೊಡನೆ ಹೋರಾಡುತ್ತಾನೆ. ರಕ್ತಸಿಕ್ತರಾದ ಇಬ್ಬರೂ ಉರಿಯುವ ಪರ್ವತಗಳಂತೆ ಹೊಳೆಯುತ್ತಾರೆ.","hi":"धृतराष्ट्र के पुत्रों को गिरा देखकर कर्ण क्रोध से भीम से बाण-प्रतिबाणों से लड़ता है। रक्त-रंजित दोनों योद्धा जलते पर्वतों की तरह दमकते हैं।","te":"ధృతరాష్ట్ర పుత్రులు పడిపోవడం చూసి కర్ణుడు కోపించి బాణ ప్రతిబాణాలతో భీమునితో పోరాడతాడు. రక్తసిక్తులైన ఇద్దరూ మండే పర్వతాల్లా ప్రకాశిస్తారు.","ta":"த்ருதராஷ்டிரனின் மக்கள் வீழ்ந்ததைக் கண்ட கர்ணன் சினந்து அம்பும் எதிரம்பும் கொண்டு பீமனுடன் போரிடுகிறான். இரத்தம் தோய்ந்த இருவரும் எரியும் மலைகள் போல் ஒளிர்கின்றனர்.","ml":"ധൃതരാഷ്ട്രരുടെ പുത്രന്മാർ വീണുകിടക്കുന്നത് കണ്ട് കർണ്ണൻ കോപിച്ച് അമ്പുകളും പ്രത്യമ്പുകളുമായി ഭീമനോട് പൊരുതുന്നു. രക്തവും മുറിവുകളും പുരണ്ട ആ രണ്ടു യോദ്ധാക്കൾ ജ്വലിക്കുന്ന പർവതങ്ങൾപോലെ തിളങ്ങുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 7.111; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Sep 22 2026","sections":[{"title":"जयद्रथवधपर्व","titleEn":"Jayadrathavadha Parva (Slaying of Jayadratha)","verses":[{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"तवात्मजांस्तु पतितान्दृष्ट्वा कर्णः प्रतापवान् ।\nक्रोधेन महताविष्टो निर्विण्णोऽभूत्स जीवितात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing your sons fallen, the mighty Karna was seized by great anger and became weary of life."}},{"n":2,"text":"आगस्कृतमिवात्मानं मेने चाधिरथिस्तदा ।\nभीमसेनं ततः क्रुद्धः समाद्रवत संभ्रमात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Adhiratha's son then felt as if he himself had committed an offense, and, angry, rushed at Bhimasena in agitation."}},{"n":3,"text":"स भीमं पञ्चभिर्विद्ध्वा राधेयः प्रहसन्निव ।\nपुनर्विव्याध सप्तत्या स्वर्णपुङ्खैः शिलाशितैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Radheya, smiling as it were, struck Bhima with five arrows, and again with seventy gold-feathered arrows whetted on stone."}},{"n":4,"text":"अवहासं तु तं पार्थो नामृष्यत वृकोदरः ।\nततो विव्याध राधेयं शतेन नतपर्वणाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Partha Vrikodara could not bear that laughter, and he struck Radheya with a hundred smooth-jointed arrows."}},{"n":5,"text":"पुनश्च विशिखैस्तीक्ष्णैर्विद्ध्वा पञ्चभिराशुगैः ।\nधनुश्चिच्छेद भल्लेन सूतपुत्रस्य मारिष ॥","meaning":{"en":"And again, having struck him with five sharp swift arrows, sir, he cut the charioteer's son's bow with a broad-headed arrow."}},{"n":6,"text":"अथान्यद्धनुरादाय कर्णो भारत दुर्मनाः ।\nइषुभिश्छादयामास भीमसेनं समन्ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Karna, O Bharata, in low spirits, took another bow and covered Bhimasena on every side with arrows."}},{"n":7,"text":"तस्य भीमो हयान्हत्वा विनिहत्य च सारथिम् ।\nप्रजहास महाहासं कृते प्रतिकृतं पुनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhima killed his horses and his charioteer, and laughed a great laugh, paying back what had been done to him."}},{"n":8,"text":"इषुभिः कार्मुकं चास्य चकर्त पुरुषर्षभः ।\nतत्पपात महाराज स्वर्णपृष्ठं महास्वनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The best of men also cut his bow with arrows; that gold-backed bow fell with a great clang, great king."}},{"n":9,"text":"अवारोहद्रथात्तस्मादथ कर्णो महारथः ।\nगदां गृहीत्वा समरे भीमसेनाय चाक्षिपत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the great chariot-warrior Karna got down from that chariot, took a mace, and threw it at Bhimasena in the battle."}},{"n":10,"text":"तामापतन्तीं सहसा गदां दृष्ट्वा वृकोदरः ।\nशरैरवारयद्राजन्सर्वसैन्यस्य पश्यतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the mace suddenly coming, Vrikodara held it off with arrows, O king, while the whole army watched."}},{"n":11,"text":"ततो बाणसहस्राणि प्रेषयामास पाण्डवः ।\nसूतपुत्रवधाकाङ्क्षी त्वरमाणः पराक्रमी ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the valiant Pandava, wishing to kill the charioteer's son, hastily shot thousands of arrows."}},{"n":12,"text":"तानिषूनिषुभिः कर्णो वारयित्वा महामृधे ।\nकवचं भीमसेनस्य पातयामास सायकैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Karna, having warded off those arrows with arrows in the great fight, struck Bhimasena's armor down with his shafts."}},{"n":13,"text":"अथैनं पञ्चविंशत्या क्षुद्रकाणां समार्पयत् ।\nपश्यतां सर्वभूतानां तदद्भुतमिवाभवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then he struck him with twenty-five small arrows, and it seemed marvelous to all beings who watched."}},{"n":14,"text":"ततो भीमो महाराज नवभिर्नतपर्वणाम् ।\nरणेऽप्रेषयत क्रुद्धः सूतपुत्रस्य मारिष ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Bhima, great king, angry, sent nine smooth-jointed arrows at the charioteer's son in the battle, sir."}},{"n":15,"text":"ते तस्य कवचं भित्त्वा तथा बाहुं च दक्षिणम् ।\nअभ्यगुर्धरणीं तीक्ष्णा वल्मीकमिव पन्नगाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Piercing his armor and his right arm, those sharp arrows went into the earth like snakes into an anthill."}},{"n":16,"text":"राधेयं तु रणे दृष्ट्वा पदातिनमवस्थितम् ।\nभीमसेनेन संरब्धं राजा दुर्योधनोऽब्रवीत् ।\nत्वरध्वं सर्वतो यत्ता राधेयस्य रथं प्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing Radheya standing on foot in the battle, attacked furiously by Bhimasena, King Duryodhana said, \"Hasten, all of you, with care, to Radheya's chariot.\""}},{"n":17,"text":"ततस्तव सुता राजञ्श्रुत्वा भ्रातुर्वचो द्रुतम् ।\nअभ्ययुः पाण्डवं युद्धे विसृजन्तः शिताञ्शरान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then your sons, O king, hearing their brother's words, quickly went at the Pandava in the battle, shooting sharp arrows."}},{"n":18,"text":"चित्रोपचित्रश्चित्राक्षश्चारुचित्रः शरासनः ।\nचित्रायुधश्चित्रवर्मा समरे चित्रयोधिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Chitra, Upachitra, Chitraksha, Charuchitra, Sharasana, Chitrayudha and Chitravarman, those fighters of marvelous method in the battle,"}},{"n":19,"text":"आगच्छतस्तान्सहसा भीमो राजन्महारथः ।\nसाश्वसूतध्वजान्यत्तान्पातयामास संयुगे ।\nते हता न्यपतन्भूमौ वातनुन्ना इव द्रुमाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"as they came suddenly, great king, Bhima, the great chariot-warrior, felled in the battle with their horses, charioteers and banners, though they were careful. Slain, they fell to the ground like trees driven by the wind."}},{"n":20,"text":"दृष्ट्वा विनिहतान्पुत्रांस्तव राजन्महारथान् ।\nअश्रुपूर्णमुखः कर्णः कश्मलं समपद्यत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing your sons, great chariot-warriors, slain, O king, Karna, his face full of tears, fell into dejection."}},{"n":21,"text":"रथमन्यं समास्थाय विधिवत्कल्पितं पुनः ।\nअभ्ययात्पाण्डवं युद्धे त्वरमाणः पराक्रमी ॥","meaning":{"en":"Mounting another chariot duly fitted out, the valiant one quickly attacked the Pandava in the battle."}},{"n":22,"text":"तावन्योन्यं शरैर्विद्ध्वा स्वर्णपुङ्खैः शिलाशितैः ।\nव्यभ्राजेतां महाराज पुष्पिताविव किंशुकौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having pierced each other with gold-feathered arrows whetted on stone, those two, great king, shone like two kimshuka trees in flower."}},{"n":23,"text":"षट्त्रिंशद्भिस्ततो भल्लैर्निशितैस्तिग्मतेजनैः ।\nव्यधमत्कवचं क्रुद्धः सूतपुत्रस्य पाण्डवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the Pandava, angry, cut the charioteer's son's armor with thirty-six sharp, keen-pointed broad-headed arrows."}},{"n":24,"text":"रक्तचन्दनदिग्धाङ्गौ शरैः कृतमहाव्रणौ ।\nशोणिताक्तौ व्यराजेतां कालसूर्याविवोदितौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Their limbs smeared with red sandal, with great wounds made by arrows and stained with blood, they shone like the sun of the end of time risen."}},{"n":25,"text":"तौ शोणितोक्षितैर्गात्रैः शरैश्छिन्नतनुच्छदौ ।\nविवर्माणौ व्यराजेतां निर्मुक्ताविव पन्नगौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"With their bodies sprinkled with blood and their armor cut away by arrows, they shone unarmored like two snakes that have shed their skins."}},{"n":26,"text":"व्याघ्राविव नरव्याघ्रौ दंष्ट्राभिरितरेतरम् ।\nशरदंष्ट्रा विधुन्वानौ ततक्षतुररिंदमौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Like two tigers, those two tigers among men, tamers of foes, shaking arrow-fangs at each other, tore at one another."}},{"n":27,"text":"वारणाविव संसक्तौ रङ्गमध्ये विरेजतुः ।\nतुदन्तौ विशिखैस्तीक्ष्णैर्मत्तवारणविक्रमौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Like two elephants locked together, they shone in the midst of the arena, pricking each other with sharp arrows, with the prowess of rutting elephants."}},{"n":28,"text":"प्रच्छादयन्तौ समरे शरजालैः परस्परम् ।\nरथाभ्यां नादयन्तौ च दिशः सर्वा विचेरतुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Covering each other with nets of arrows in the battle, making the directions resound with their chariots, they ranged everywhere."}},{"n":29,"text":"तौ रथाभ्यां महाराज मण्डलावर्तनादिषु ।\nव्यरोचेतां महात्मानौ वृत्रवज्रधराविव ॥","meaning":{"en":"In turnings and circlings with their chariots, great king, those two great-souled men shone like Vritra and the bearer of the thunderbolt."}},{"n":30,"text":"सहस्ताभरणाभ्यां तु भुजाभ्यां विक्षिपन्धनुः ।\nव्यरोचत रणे भीमः सविद्युदिव तोयदः ॥","meaning":{"en":"With his arms adorned with gloves and ornaments, as he drew his bow, Bhima shone in the battle like a cloud with lightning."}},{"n":31,"text":"स चापघोषस्तनितः शरधाराम्बुदो महान् ।\nभीममेघो महाराज कर्णपर्वतमभ्ययात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"With the twang of the bow as thunder and the showers of arrows as rain, that great Bhima-cloud advanced on the Karna-mountain, great king."}},{"n":32,"text":"ततः शरसहस्रेण धनुर्मुक्तेन भारत ।\nपाण्डवो व्यकिरत्कर्णं घनोऽद्रिमिव वृष्टिभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, O Bharata, the Pandava heaped Karna with a thousand arrows loosed from his bow, as a cloud pours rain on a mountain."}},{"n":33,"text":"तत्रावैक्षन्त पुत्रास्ते भीमसेनस्य विक्रमम् ।\nसुपुङ्खैः कङ्कवासोभिर्यत्कर्णं छादयच्छरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"There your sons watched Bhimasena's prowess, in that he covered Karna with well-feathered arrows with heron plumes."}},{"n":34,"text":"स नन्दयन्रणे पार्थं केशवं च यशस्विनम् ।\nसात्यकिं चक्ररक्षौ च भीमः कर्णमयोधयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Gladdening Partha and the renowned Keshava, and Satyaki and the two wheel-guards, Bhima fought Karna."}},{"n":35,"text":"विक्रमं भुजयोर्वीर्यं धैर्यं च विदितात्मनः ।\nपुत्रास्तव महाराज ददृशुः पाण्डवस्य ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Your sons, great king, saw the prowess, the arm-strength and the steadiness of the self-possessed Pandava."}}]}]}